WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.620
One click

2
00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:01.650
ends your checkout.

3
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.050
Beneath that button,

4
00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:04.350
an unseen factory

5
00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:05.300
starts running.

6
00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:06.720
Most buyers think

7
00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.000
sites just autofill cards.

8
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.400
Amazon's 1999

9
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.900
US Patent 5,960,411

10
00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:13.950
expired in September 2017.

11
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:15.720
Yet modern speed

12
00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.450
hides raw numbers.

13
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:18.850
A silent relay

14
00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:20.000
links encrypted keys

15
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.550
straight to loading docks.

16
00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:23.020
It starts before

17
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:24.100
your cursor moves.

18
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:25.320
Visa Token Service

19
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:26.280
and Mastercard swap

20
00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:27.320
your raw card number

21
00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:28.440
for a cryptographic token.

22
00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:29.660
Each one binds

23
00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:30.450
to your profile

24
00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:31.700
and default address.

25
00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:33.240
Still, tokens alone

26
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:34.250
never clear payment.

27
00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:35.650
Hit buy.

28
00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.000
An API sends

29
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.040
your SKU and token

30
00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:38.900
to the gateway.

31
00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:40.480
Machine-learning fraud models

32
00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:41.700
score device and transaction

33
00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:42.900
signals in about

34
00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:44.650
200 to 300 milliseconds.

35
00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:46.360
Bank authorization clears

36
00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:47.550
faster than a blink.

37
00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:48.920
But approval cannot

38
00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:50.000
pack boxes.

39
00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:51.760
So the Order Management

40
00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:52.560
System syncs with

41
00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:53.550
the Warehouse Management System.

42
00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.200
Live stock locks.

43
00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:56.240
Software picks

44
00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:57.050
the nearest warehouse,

45
00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:58.380
generating a carrier label

46
00:00:58.380 --> 00:00:59.050
via API

47
00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:00.800
before the tab closes.

48
00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:02.400
Delivery trucks still

49
00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:03.350
need real miles.

50
00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:05.450
One click feels effortless

51
00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:07.080
because an invisible architecture

52
00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.650
finished sprinting first.
